Task 3: Locator Strategies
Write locator strategies for 5 different elements on the home screen of your sample app. Each element should have at least two locator types.

Example Code:

python
# 1. Login Button
driver.find_element_by_id("com.example.app:id/login")
driver.find_element_by_xpath("//android.widget.Button[@text='Login']")

# 2. Settings Icon
driver.find_element_by_accessibility_id("Settings")
driver.find_element_by_class_name("android.widget.ImageView")

# 3. Search Box
driver.find_element_by_id("com.example.app:id/search")
driver.find_element_by_xpath("//android.widget.EditText[@content-desc='search_box']")

# 4. Profile Picture
driver.find_element_by_accessibility_id("Profile")
driver.find_element_by_class_name("android.widget.ImageView")

# 5. Logout Button
driver.find_element_by_id("com.example.app:id/logout")
driver.find_element_by_xpath("//android.widget.Button[@text='Logout']")
Description:

id and resource-id are the most stable locators.

accessibilityId is useful for accessibility-friendly apps.

className and xpath are fallback options when unique IDs are missing.

Task 4: Element Hierarchy & XPath
Use Appium Inspector to capture the full element hierarchy.

Write XPath expressions for parent, child, and sibling relationships.

Example Code:

python
# Parent element
driver.find_element_by_xpath("//android.widget.LinearLayout")

# Child element
driver.find_element_by_xpath("//android.widget.LinearLayout/android.widget.TextView")

# Sibling element
driver.find_element_by_xpath("//android.widget.TextView[@text='Username']/following-sibling::android.widget.EditText")

# Nested button inside layout
driver.find_element_by_xpath("//android.widget.LinearLayout/android.widget.Button[@text='Submit']")
Description:

XPath allows navigation through nested layouts.

Parent-child-sibling relationships help target elements when IDs are missing.

Task 5: Reliable Locators
Inspect 3 interactive elements and decide which locator is most reliable.

Example Notes:

Login Button → id is most reliable because it’s unique and stable across updates.

Username Input Box → resource-id is best since placeholder text may change but ID remains constant.

Dark Mode Toggle → accessibilityId is reliable because accessibility labels are designed to remain stable.
